@startuml commit_addition_limit
' Pre-change source evidence: .github/workflows/ci.yml:3-7,13,15-26 at c9d858bc8261bf07f5585f545b53495bf2226a56.
' Reviewed implementation evidence: scripts/check-commit-additions.sh:40-202 and scripts/tests/check-commit-additions-test.sh:86-234 at 93a0c11952218cb03cb4f9b89927e2280820dbce.
' Observed behavior: CI checked formatting and the Maven build without a commit-size gate.
' Architecture change: the gate checks normal and merge-only commit additions and fails closed.
' Design reason: bound reviewable commit size without charging documentation or target history.
title Per-commit addition limit

actor Contributor
participant "GitHub Actions" as Actions
database "Git history" as Git
participant "Commit addition gate" as Gate
participant "Existing build gates" as Build

Contributor -> Actions: Push pull-request commits
Actions -> Git: Checkout full history
Actions -> Gate: Provide base SHA and head SHA
Gate -> Git: Resolve merge base

loop Each commit
  Gate -> Git: Read commit parents
  alt Zero or one parent
    Gate -> Git: Read rename-aware diff-tree numstat
  else Two parents
    Gate -> Git: Read remerge-diff numstat
  else More than two parents
    Gate --> Actions: Fail closed as unsupported
  end
  Gate -> Gate: Classify old and new paths
  opt Documentation moved into code
    Gate -> Git: Read full destination blob
  end
  Gate -> Gate: Sum added lines only
  alt Added code lines exceed 2000
    Gate --> Actions: Fail with commit and file details
  else Added code lines are at most 2000
    Gate --> Actions: Report commit pass
  end
end

Actions -> Gate: Run gate regression tests
Actions -> Build: Set up JDK, format check, verify
Build --> Contributor: CI result
@enduml
